# With no tracker configured, an id is prose — and stays prose.
#
# Same thread and the same point as tracker_links.e2e, with the tracker host
# unset (the default: no host is compiled into this client anywhere). Pressing
# the id must do nothing at all. A link that opens nothing is worse than the
# text it replaced, so the absence here is the feature.
#
# NOTE: expect_no_text takes a BARE single word — see afterhours_gaps.md #47.
#
# THE POINT MUST BE ON THE ID. It was (456,492) — 348px below the only tracker
# id in this thread, which is to say on nothing. A negative test that clicks
# empty space passes whatever the app does, and this one did: with the host
# check deleted from link_hotspot (`if (app == nullptr) return {}`), so that
# every id becomes a link and clicking one raises the toast with no host
# configured, the old coordinate still passed. The point below is the same one
# tracker_links clicks, measured with HANABI_LINK_AUDIT=1, so this test now
# asks "the id is there, the click lands on it, and nothing opens" rather than
# "nothing opens when you click the background".
#
# env: HANABI_LINK_AUDIT=1
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t1"],"active_tab":"t1","theme":"dark"}

expect_text "Built the config diff"

mouse_move 455 147
wait_frames 4
click 455 147
wait_frames 10
expect_no_text Opened
expect_text "Built the config diff"
